# MANIFEST.md5 -- static 0x44EE76D5, mint 3 RC2: the FIELDED Linux harness (MicroBlaze V, Vivado 2026.1).
#
# `md5sum -c MANIFEST.md5` from inside this directory. Two sets, one static:
#
# (1) THE MINT'S SET -- generated 2026-09-28 (lane KIT-RC2) from the preserved mint, lx fb1f8c7
#     (feat/linux-harness, clean): fpga/dfx/build_mint3_rc2/{prod,shell_proj} (static_canon.json at
#     its root), and on the hub at <hub-host>:<hub-home>/mints/0x44EE76D5/ (stage-8 set, copied
#     2026-09-25). static_routed_locked.dcp is the one that matters: every RM ever built for this
#     static links against it (its CRC-32 IS the static_id).
#     RENAMED IN THIS RECORD at the cutover (fetch_fielded.sh maps them back to their source names):
#       config_rm_greybox_stage0_mint.bit  <- the mint's own bake, stored as config_rm_greybox_stage0.bit
#       stage0_bake_mint.json              <- the mint's stage0_bake.json
#     because config_rm_greybox_stage0.bit / stage0_bake.json in a fielded record are "what the board
#     boots", which linux_bundle.json and scripts/harness_gates/check_image_overlay_match.py hold it to.
#
# (2) THE FIELDED SET -- the per-board config-SD bits and the release image. Not in the mint's build
#     dir: built by the stage0 re-bakes of 2026-09-28 (updatemem, BRAM + CRC frames only: static_id,
#     UserID 0xFB1F8C76 and USR_ACCESS 0x01000000 are the mint's) and the clean image build of
#     2026-09-28 (ad297bf, dirty=0). Hub copy: <hub-home>/mints/0x44EE76D5/fielded/ (made at the
#     cutover, C3; before that the files are in <hub-home>/pv_field/ and the Linux lead's lanes).
#       config_rm_greybox_stage0.bit          BOARD 1 (<board-1 target>) config SD since 2026-09-28 21:10
#                                             sha256 f876e73e412c35b65130a7966819d63cce3ec1f5aa5b6e8f9838f43c7a9660ba
#                                             stage0 build 0x34956F94 (cd767ae cold-start fix + 34956f9 identity),
#                                             label MPS3-01, 192.168.10.101, MAC 02:00:00:4D:50:53
#       stage0_field_b1.elf                   the stage0 in it (sha256 7612bfc5afe8...)
#       config_rm_greybox_stage0_b2.bit       BOARD 2 (<board-2 target>) config SD NOW (since 2026-09-28)
#                                             sha256 f206f788f7497b650b6f0408ebb2fbdb795edb749784a3ec42e6caaaa3df5058
#                                             stage0 build 0x6FAE6A0B: rescue IP <board-2 IP> only, NO cold-start
#                                             fix, NO identity publish (shows board 1's MAC under Linux)
#       stage0_b2.elf                         the stage0 in it (sha256 1bbfc229caf3...)
#       config_rm_greybox_stage0_field_b2.bit BOARD 2's NEXT bake, built, NOT FIELDED (needs PB0 cover on site)
#                                             sha256 d7d0d37601843df2a99aa4429c43b5033050f216082d7133b632eddff3356015
#                                             stage0 build 0x34956F94, label MPS3-02, <board-2 IP>, MAC 02:00:00:00:02:FE
#       stage0_field_b2.elf                   the stage0 in it (sha256 d62a4bbfe5c1...)
#       linux_slot.img                        rc2_v7, the card image (both slots of board 1 since 2026-09-29)
#                                             sha256 05c83617bfac30c6c66a09dc946b2243cb9112692a9afa2d8352bcba054569ea
#       linux_slot_v7n.img                    rc2_v7n, the netboot image (board 2 via b2_keeper; persist=off)
#                                             sha256 65b6bbaf16171c10aaef80c5f44aab2b93800400183b0e2c7613456aec059680
#       linux_legal_info.tar                  Buildroot legal-info for rc2_v7/v7n (GPL: travels with every copy)
#                                             sha256 5ae61c197d2578185c62b732e76e5e50d153aabd96fec65b08f876737c562375
#       linux_bundle.json (tracked)           the release manifest, sha256 333a69704437...; it names BOARD 1's pair
#       stage0_bake.json (tracked)            board 1's bake record (was the mint's; see (1))
#       stage0_bake_b2.json, stage0_bake_field_b2.json (tracked)   board 2's current and next bake records
#
# Not listed: the RC2 re-bake of 2026-09-26 (sha256 286ae54d..., stage0 build 0xC457D656,
# stage0_bake_rebake.json). It was on board 1's config SD from 2026-09-26 to 2026-09-28 21:10 and is on
# no board now; no copy of the bit is archived. The 13 Linux overlays (overlay_mbv/) are not listed
# either: make fielded-files keeps only the .ltx-bearing RMs' pairs, so C3 copies overlay_mbv/ to the
# hub beside this set (CUTOVER_RUNBOOK_LINUX.md C3).
#
